+/// Classify a `put_fragment` error status (issue #638): `FAILED_PRECONDITION`
+/// reconstructs [`WriteDeadlineExpired`] — the D server's refusal of a write whose
+/// authorization deadline had already elapsed when it tried to apply it (0016
+/// decision 5) — so a caller can tell "refused, too late" apart from a genuine
+/// backend fault (`wyrd_traits::is_write_deadline_expired`), the same trick
+/// `classify_get_status` already plays for `get_fragment`'s two fault categories.
+/// `put_fragment`'s other special status, `INVALID_ARGUMENT` (a malformed
+/// fragment, `server.rs`), is not reconstructed to a typed seam error here — it
+/// already surfaces distinctly via the wire `Status` code itself, unchanged from
+/// before this issue. Everything else falls to [`transport_error`]'s generic
+/// mapping (the transient trio, and the fail-safe terminal default).
+fn classify_put_status(id: FragmentId, status: Status) -> BoxError {
+    match status.code() {
+        Code::FailedPrecondition => Box::new(WriteDeadlineExpired {
+            id,
+            detail: status.message().to_string(),
+        }),
+        _ => transport_error(status),
+    }
+}
